# Cliff₃ derives the decoded refined qutrit relations (Appendices C, F.3, G.3)

The derivations of Appendix C, each replayed line by line from the paper's
figures, then the decoding of every rule of the refined source (`RRule`:
Li et al.'s C1–C18 read with `-ω = ω₁₂¹⁰`, and `ω₁₂¹² = 1`; Appendix G.3,
`rel_derivable`) and the round trips of the generators (Appendix F.3, `DE`).
Each step between two printed lines was found by a search over rewrites
modulo commuting gates on disjoint wires, using the rules the paper cites
for that step (and their derived forms), and is replayed by `derive`.

The figures of Appendix C are not always exact: several lines carry the
scalar of the misprinted (E) (`ω₁₂⁷` for `ω₁₂`), or drop a scalar, and in
(ZK) `Z` is spelt `S S'²`, which is `Z⁻¹` for Figure 9's `Z = S² S'`.  Such
lines are corrected by their phase, or skipped when not a multiple of the
first line (`gen/driver.py`, `repair`); the figure `Kb-CNOT-03` cited in
(KbCnot) is missing from the paper's sources and its step is merged with
the next.  The decoded `CZ`, `H³ CNOT H`, is symmetric by (dczrev), the
square of the CZ of (CzRev).

Generated by `gen/gen_cliff3.py` from the derivations `gen/run_cliff3.py`
finds (the figures read by `gen/figparse.py`).
-/
import QCert.Minimality.QutritClifford.Transfer
